    "objectID": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html",
    "href": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html",
    "title": "1  Prior Knowledge Integration",
    "section": "",
    "text": "1.1 Installation\nariadne (R) and ariadnepy (Python) give access to the same resource: a single graph assembled from public biological databases (Gene Ontology, KEGG, UniProt, BugSigDB, ChocoPhlAn, and more), which can be queried and traversed to link one type of biological identifier to another — for example, taxonomic names to functional pathways, or gene families to disease modules.\nThis page walks through the same short analysis twice, once in R and once in Python, so you can follow along in whichever language you use.",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Prior Knowledge Integration</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#installation",
    "href": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#installation",
    "title": "1  Prior Knowledge Integration",
    "section": "",
    "text": "RPython\n\n\n\nremotes::install_github(\"Minotau-R/ariadne\")\n\n\n\n\npip install ariadnepy",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Prior Knowledge Integration</span>"
    ]
