  {
    "objectID": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#building-the-resource-graph",
    "href": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#building-the-resource-graph",
    "title": "1  Prior Knowledge Integration",
    "section": "1.2 Building the resource graph",
    "text": "1.2 Building the resource graph\nBoth packages expose a single entry point that downloads (and locally caches) the resource graph.\n\nRPython\n\n\n\nlibrary(ariadne)\n\ngraph &lt;- ariadne()\nsummary(graph)\n##  IGRAPH c68c211 DN-- 202 545 -- \n##  + attr: name (v/c), BugSigDB (v/c), ChocoPhlAn (v/c), GM (v/c), GO\n##  | (v/c), KEGG (v/c), MSigDB (v/c), OTT (v/c), Rhea (v/c), TIGRFAMs\n##  | (v/c), UniProt (v/c), WoL (v/c), source (v/c), url (v/c), source\n##  | (e/c), url (e/c)\n\n\n\n\nimport ariadnepy\n\ngraph = ariadnepy.ariadne()\nprint(graph.summary())\n##  IGRAPH UN-- 202 545 -- \n##  + attr: versions (g), id (v), name (v), specific (v), url (v), source (e), url (e)",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Prior Knowledge Integration</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#searching-for-paths",
    "href": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#searching-for-paths",
    "title": "1  Prior Knowledge Integration",
    "section": "1.3 Searching for paths",
    "text": "1.3 Searching for paths\nBefore linking two resources, it helps to see which routes connect them. searchPath() / search_path() print the first k shortest paths.\n\nRPython\n\n\n\nsearchPath(graph, ko ~ ec, k = 3)\n##  Path 1:\n##  ko -(KEGG)-&gt; ec\n##  \n##  Path 2:\n##  ko -(ChocoPhlAn)-&gt; uniref90 -(UniProt)-&gt; ec\n##  \n##  Path 3:\n##  ko -(ChocoPhlAn)-&gt; uniref50 -(UniProt)-&gt; ec\n\n\n\n\nariadnepy.search_path(graph, \"ko ~ ec\", k=3)\n##  Path 1:\n##    ko -(KEGG)-&gt; ec\n##  \n##  Path 2:\n##    ko -(KEGG)-&gt; kegg_rxn -(KEGG)-&gt; ec\n##  \n##  Path 3:\n##    ko -(ChocoPhlAn)-&gt; uniref50 -(UniProt)-&gt; ec",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Prior Knowledge Integration</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#visualising-a-path",
    "href": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#visualising-a-path",
    "title": "1  Prior Knowledge Integration",
    "section": "1.4 Visualising a path",
    "text": "1.4 Visualising a path\nplotPath() / plot_path() draw the full resource graph, highlighting a chosen path in red.\n\nRPython\n\n\n\nplotPath(graph, ko ~ ec, k = 1, prune = TRUE, focus = TRUE)\n##  Warning in matrix(c(0, rep(0, dim - 1), 1, rep(0, dim - 2)), 2, dim, byrow =\n##  TRUE): data length [3] is not a sub-multiple or multiple of the number of\n##  rows [2]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nfig = ariadnepy.plot_path(graph, \"ko ~ ec\", k=1, prune=True, focus=True)\nfig",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Prior Knowledge Integration</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#weaving-a-linkmap",
    "href": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#weaving-a-linkmap",
    "title": "1  Prior Knowledge Integration",
    "section": "1.5 Weaving a linkmap",
    "text": "1.5 Weaving a linkmap\nweavePath() / weave_path() traverse the chosen path and return a two-column table mapping origin identifiers to target identifiers.\n\nRPython\n\n\n\nko2ec &lt;- weavePath(graph, ko ~ ec, k = 1)\n##  ko -(KEGG)-&gt; ec\n##  Warning: names for 3 ec ids not found.\nhead(ko2ec)\n##        ko      ec               ec.name\n##  1 K00001 1.1.1.1 alcohol dehydrogenase\n##  2 K00121 1.1.1.1 alcohol dehydrogenase\n##  3 K04072 1.1.1.1 alcohol dehydrogenase\n##  4 K11440 1.1.1.1 alcohol dehydrogenase\n##  5 K13951 1.1.1.1 alcohol dehydrogenase\n##  6 K13952 1.1.1.1 alcohol dehydrogenase\n\n\n\n\nko2ec = ariadnepy.weave_path(graph, \"ko ~ ec\", k=1)\n##    ko -(KEGG)-&gt; ec\n##  C:\\aditi\\ariadnePy\\src\\ariadnepy\\graph\\_weave.py:984: UserWarning: 3 ec ids not found.\n##    name_map = link_names(graph, to, list(result[to]))\nko2ec.head()\n##         ko         ec                                   ec.name\n##  0  K00001    1.1.1.1                     alcohol dehydrogenase\n##  1  K00002    1.1.1.2             alcohol dehydrogenase (NADP+)\n##  2  K00003    1.1.1.3                  homoserine dehydrogenase\n##  3  K00004  1.1.1.303  diacetyl reductase [(R)-acetoin forming]\n##  4  K00004    1.1.1.4            (R,R)-butanediol dehydrogenase\n\n\n\n\nweavePath() / weave_path() also accept a fixed path table (e.g. from drawPath() / draw_path(), see below) instead of the full graph, which skips path search entirely and re-runs just those steps — useful once you’ve settled on a route and want to reuse it with different init IDs.",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Prior Knowledge Integration</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#reproducibility-recording-the-path-used",
    "href": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#reproducibility-recording-the-path-used",
    "title": "1  Prior Knowledge Integration",
    "section": "1.6 Reproducibility: recording the path used",
    "text": "1.6 Reproducibility: recording the path used\ndrawPath() / draw_path() return the resource, version, and URL used at every hop of a path — handy for citing the exact data sources behind a result.\n\nRPython\n\n\n\ndrawPath(graph, ko ~ ec, k = 1)\n##    from to source version  url\n##  1   ko ec   KEGG  latest &lt;NA&gt;\n\n\n\n\nariadnepy.draw_path(graph, \"ko ~ ec\", k=1)\n##    from  to source version  url\n##  0   ko  ec   KEGG  latest  NaN",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Prior Knowledge Integration</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#python-only-annotating-anndata-objects",
    "href": "pages/prior-knowledge-integration.html#python-only-annotating-anndata-objects",
    "title": "1  Prior Knowledge Integration",
    "section": "1.7 Python only: annotating AnnData objects",
    "text": "1.7 Python only: annotating AnnData objects\nariadnepy additionally provides add_modules() / get_modules(), which attach a linkmap as module-membership columns directly onto an AnnData object’s var (features) or obs (samples) metadata — no R equivalent is needed here since AnnData is Python-specific. Any two-column linkmap works, whether it comes from weave_path()/weave_complex() or from elsewhere; the example below builds one by hand from the bundled butyrate-producer dataset, so it runs without any network access.\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\n\nbutyrate = ariadnepy.load_butyrate()\n\nadata = ad.AnnData(\n    X=np.zeros((1, len(butyrate))),\n    var=butyrate.set_index(\"taxname\"),\n)\n\n# A minimal linkmap: taxon -&gt; a butyrate-production module ID.\nlinkmap = butyrate[[\"taxname\"]].assign(module=\"M_BUTYRATE\")\n\nadata = ariadnepy.add_modules(adata, linkmap, key=\"index\")\nadata.var.head()\n##                             cpd  cpd.name  M_BUTYRATE\n##  taxname                                             \n##  Butyricimonas           C00246  butyrate         1.0\n##  Odoribacter             C00246  butyrate         1.0\n##  Agathobacter            C00246  butyrate         1.0\n##  Anaerobutyricum         C00246  butyrate         1.0\n##  Eubacterium ventriosum  C00246  butyrate         1.0",
    "crumbs": [
      "<span class='chapter-number'>1</span>  <span class='chapter-title'>Prior Knowledge Integration</span>"
    ]
  },
  {
